---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description={`About ${SITE.title}`}>
  <article class="reading">
    <header class="post-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="post-desc">Gear, money, and the everyday - tested by our family.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="post-content">
      <p>
        Hi, I'm Jason. My wife and I are raising two kids, plus a dog who's convinced
        he's the third. By day I build products for software companies and run a small
        business. pastelloclub is where that life runs into parenthood.
      </p>
      <p>
        I can't out-parent the internet, so I stick to what I know: test things
        properly, take honest notes, and share them. Around here that means three
        kinds of writing:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Gear reviews written like product teardowns - what held up, what broke, and
          whether it earns its shelf space. We rate everything on the Pastello Scale.
        </li>
        <li>
          Money notes for parents who work for themselves - Trump accounts, 529s, and
          budgeting on a variable income.
        </li>
        <li>
          Everyday notes - feeding small humans, surviving sleep
          regressions, the quiet ten minutes after they finally close their eyes.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Everything comes from things we actually own, actually paid for, and actually
        live with - usually for years. When something's a dud, I'll say so. Some links
        are affiliate links; the opinions aren't for sale.
      </p>
      <p>
        No tracking, no popups, no recipes that start with a 1,500-word memoir.
        Just notes, in pastel.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want to say hello? Write us at
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
